    dcterms:description "Integration machine that reads combined output signals from the Benefits Eligibility Screener [952:956] and the Service Intake Assessment Monitor [956:960] to detect enrollment coordination failures — cases where eligible, assessed clients are not transitioning into active services. The gap between confirmed eligibility and actual enrollment is the most significant service delivery failure in community programs: eligible people who never get enrolled. Output at [984:988] is available to downstream care coordination systems." ;
